{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++11 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <cstring>\n#include <algorithm>\nconst int MAXN = 50 + 10;\nconst int MOD = 1e9 + 7;\ntypedef long long LL;\n\nLL n;\nint k;\nnamespace {\n  inline int add(int x) { return x >= MOD ? x - MOD : x; }\n  inline int sub(int x) { return x < 0 ? x + MOD : x; }\n  inline int mul(int x, int y) { return (long long) x * y % MOD; }\n}\nnamespace solver1 {\n  struct Matrix {\n    int a[MAXN][MAXN];\n    int n;\n    void init() { memset(a, 0, sizeof a); }\n    void set() {\n      init() ;\n      for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {\n        a[i][i] = 1;\n      }\n    }\n    Matrix operator * (const Matrix &rhs) const {\n      Matrix ans;\n      ans.n = n;\n      static long long tmp[MAXN][MAXN];\n      static const long long MODLL = (LL) MOD * MOD;\n      for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {\n        for (int j = 1; j <= n; j++) {\n          tmp[i][j] = 0;\n        }\n      }\n      for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {\n        for (int k = 1; k <= n; k++) {\n          for (int j = 1; j <= n; j++) {\n            tmp[i][j] += (LL) a[i][k] * rhs.a[k][j];\n            if (tmp[i][j] >= MODLL) tmp[i][j] -= MODLL;\n          }\n        }\n      }\n\n      for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {\n        for (int j = 1; j <= n; j++) {\n          ans.a[i][j] = tmp[i][j] % MOD;\n        }\n      }\n\n      return ans;\n    }\n  };\n  Matrix f[80][MAXN], sump[80][MAXN], sums[80][MAXN];\n  void main() {\n    static int num[80], cnt = 0;\n\n    while(n) {\n      num[++cnt] = n % k;\n      n /= k;\n    }\n    \n    for (int i = 0; i < k; i++) {\n      f[0][i].n = k + 1;\n      f[0][i].init();\n      for (int j = 1; j <= k + 1; j++) {\n        f[0][i].a[j][j] = 1;\n        f[0][i].a[i + 1][j] = 1;\n      }\n    }\n    sump[0][0] = f[0][0];\n    sums[0][k - 1] = f[0][k - 1];\n    \n    for (int i = 1; i < k; i++) {\n      sump[0][i] = f[0][i] * sump[0][i - 1];\n    }\n\n    for (int i = k - 2; i >= 0; i--) {\n      sums[0][i] = sums[0][i + 1] * f[0][i];\n    }\n\n    for (int i = 1; i < cnt; i++) {\n      for (int j = 0; j < k; j++) {\n        f[i][j] = j == 0 ? sums[i - 1][j] : sump[i - 1][j - 1] * sums[i - 1][j];\n      }\n      \n      sump[i][0] = f[i][0];\n      sums[i][k - 1] = f[i][k - 1];\n      for (int j = 1; j < k; j++) {\n        sump[i][j] = f[i][j] * sump[i][j - 1];\n      }\n      \n      for (int j = k - 2; j >= 0; j--) {\n        sums[i][j] = sums[i][j + 1] * f[i][j];\n      }\n    }\n\n    Matrix ans;\n    ans.n = k + 1;\n    ans.set();\n\n\n    int sum = 0;\n    for (int i = cnt; i >= 1; i--) {\n      for (int j = 0; j < num[i]; j++) {\n        ans = f[i - 1][(sum + j) % k] * ans;\n      }\n      sum += num[i];\n      sum %= k;\n    }\n    //ans = f[0][(sum + num[1]) % k] * ans;\n\n    int res = 0;\n    for (int i = 1; i <= k + 1; i++) {\n      res = add(res + ans.a[i][k + 1]);\n    }\n\n    printf(\"%d\\n\", res);\n    \n  }\n}\nint main() {\n  scanf(\"%lld%d\", &n, &k);\n\n  solver1::main();\n}\n\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\n\nMOD = 10**9 + 7\n\ndef add(x):\n    return x if x < MOD else x - MOD\n\ndef sub(x):\n    return x if x >= 0 else x + MOD\n\ndef mul(x, y):\n    return (x * y) % MOD\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.readline().split()\n    n = int(data[0])\n    k = int(data[1])\n    \n    MAXN = 60  # 50 + 10\n    \n    class Matrix:\n        def __init__(self, n_val=None):\n            self.n = n_val if n_val is not None else 0\n            self.a = [[0] * (MAXN + 1) for _ in range(MAXN + 1)]\n        \n        def init(self):\n            for i in range(MAXN + 1):\n                for j in range(MAXN + 1):\n                    self.a[i][j] = 0\n        \n        def set_identity(self):\n            self.init()\n            for i in range(1, self.n + 1):\n                self.a[i][i] = 1\n        \n        def __mul__(self, rhs):\n            ans = Matrix()\n            ans.n = self.n\n            tmp = [[0] * (MAXN + 1) for _ in range(MAXN + 1)]\n            MODLL = MOD * MOD\n            \n            for i in range(1, self.n + 1):\n                for j in range(1, self.n + 1):\n                    tmp[i][j] = 0\n            \n            for i in range(1, self.n + 1):\n                for k in range(1, self.n + 1):\n                    for j in range(1, self.n + 1):\n                        tmp[i][j] += self.a[i][k] * rhs.a[k][j]\n                        if tmp[i][j] >= MODLL:\n                            tmp[i][j] -= MODLL\n            \n            for i in range(1, self.n + 1):\n                for j in range(1, self.n + 1):\n                    ans.a[i][j] = tmp[i][j] % MOD\n            \n            return ans\n    \n    # Convert n to base k\n    num = []\n    temp_n = n\n    while temp_n:\n        num.append(temp_n % k)\n        temp_n //= k\n    cnt = len(num)\n    \n    # Initialize f, sump, sums arrays\n    f = [[None] * k for _ in range(80)]\n    sump = [[None] * k for _ in range(80)]\n    sums = [[None] * k for _ in range(80)]\n    \n    # Initialize f[0][i]\n    for i in range(k):\n        f[0][i] = Matrix(k + 1)\n        f[0][i].init()\n        for j in range(1, k + 2):\n            f[0][i].a[j][j] = 1\n            f[0][i].a[i + 1][j] = 1\n    \n    sump[0][0] = f[0][0]\n    sums[0][k - 1] = f[0][k - 1]\n    \n    for i in range(1, k):\n        sump[0][i] = f[0][i] * sump[0][i - 1]\n    \n    for i in range(k - 2, -1, -1):\n        sums[0][i] = sums[0][i + 1] * f[0][i]\n    \n    for i in range(1, cnt):\n        for j in range(k):\n            if j == 0:\n                f[i][j] = sums[i - 1][j]\n            else:\n                f[i][j] = sump[i - 1][j - 1] * sums[i - 1][j]\n        \n        sump[i][0] = f[i][0]\n        sums[i][k - 1] = f[i][k - 1]\n        \n        for j in range(1, k):\n            sump[i][j] = f[i][j] * sump[i][j - 1]\n        \n        for j in range(k - 2, -1, -1):\n            sums[i][j] = sums[i][j + 1] * f[i][j]\n    \n    ans = Matrix(k + 1)\n    ans.set_identity()\n    \n    total_sum = 0\n    for i in range(cnt - 1, -1, -1):\n        digit = num[i]\n        for j in range(digit):\n            ans = f[i][(total_sum + j) % k] * ans\n        total_sum += digit\n        total_sum %= k\n    \n    res = 0\n    for i in range(1, k + 2):\n        res = add(res + ans.a[i][k + 1])\n    \n    print(res)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.0001538873475510627, -8.344646857949556e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, -0.02140982449054718, -0.00026294111739844084, -0.008650803938508034, -0.007414205931127071, 0.0, -4.017272294731811e-05, 0.0, -2.264974000354414e-06, -0.0025991962756961584, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -9.536738616588991e-07, -0.34844693541526794, -0.004102861508727074, -0.01568129099905491, -0.0005109196645207703, -6.890059739816934e-05, -5.960462772236497e-07, -8.344646857949556e-07, -4.768370445162873e-07, -0.5859967470169067, -1.9073468138230965e-06, -4.5536911784438416e-05, -2.0265558760002023e-06, -2.503